# CRITICAL: -text means "store the bytes exactly as committed, never convert".
#
# Do NOT use `text eol=crlf` here. That stores LF in the repo and only converts
# on checkout - which means a GitHub "Download ZIP" hands the user an LF-only
# .bat file. cmd.exe on a CJK (cp949) console then mis-parses it: `setlocal`
# reads as `tlocal`, delayed expansion never turns on, and every `!errorlevel!`
# blows up as an unknown command. With -text the CRLF bytes are what's stored,
# so clone AND zip download both get a working file.
*.bat -text
*.cmd -text
*.ps1 -text

# POSIX shell scripts must stay LF or bash trips on the trailing CR.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary - line-ending machinery must never touch these.
*.pt binary
mobile_sam.pt binary
